-High-fat.

2171
01:22:15,630 --> 01:22:17,666
-It looks so good.
-That has to be good.

2172
01:22:18,767 --> 01:22:22,070
-She just let out a sigh.
-That was a sigh.

2173
01:22:22,137 --> 01:22:24,406
-Is that positive or negative?
-Right?

2174
01:22:24,472 --> 01:22:26,841
-Was it that good?
-Or is it…

2175
01:22:26,908 --> 01:22:29,911
First of all, it's unbelievably good.

2176
01:22:29,978 --> 01:22:32,514
But it's also a total junk food.

2177
01:22:32,580 --> 01:22:33,782
Do you feel guilty?

2178
01:22:33,848 --> 01:22:35,750
-I do feel guilty.
-I see.

2179
01:22:35,817 --> 01:22:37,953
-She feels guilty for eating it.
-But this is

2180
01:22:38,019 --> 01:22:40,188
made with sourdough and shrimp.

2181
01:22:40,255 --> 01:22:42,490
-So it's fine, right?
-It is.

2182
01:22:42,557 --> 01:22:46,695
But compared to your usual diet,
you feel like you're committing a crime.

2183
01:22:46,761 --> 01:22:48,196
That's not the case.

2184
01:22:48,263 --> 01:22:49,364
That is the case.

2185
01:22:49,431 --> 01:22:51,466
-You are not guilty.
-Say it louder.

2186
01:22:51,533 --> 01:22:53,768
-That is the case.
-Sam has something to say.

2187
01:22:53,835 --> 01:22:55,437
I thought she'd feel guilty.

2188
01:22:55,503 --> 01:22:57,906
No way. There's no need for that.

2189
01:22:57,973 --> 01:22:59,174
It was delicious.

2190
01:22:59,240 --> 01:23:00,742
Why don't we all try it?

2191
01:23:00,809 --> 01:23:03,979
-Try some, Sooyoung.
-Thank you.

2192
01:23:04,546 --> 01:23:05,580
What is this?

2193
01:23:05,647 --> 01:23:06,815
This is my seat, right?

2194
01:23:06,881 --> 01:23:08,183
HAPPY

2195
01:23:08,249 --> 01:23:09,751
You might take your uniform off to eat.

2196
01:23:09,818 --> 01:23:12,821
I should really just
come as a guest at this point.

2197
01:23:12,887 --> 01:23:14,522
-It's a feast.
-Wow.

2198
01:23:14,589 --> 01:23:16,891
-A feast.
-Yes.

2199
01:23:16,958 --> 01:23:18,760
-People will think we're the guests.
-This one first.

2200
01:23:18,827 --> 01:23:21,029
Please try it, Sooyoung.

2201
01:23:21,596 --> 01:23:22,664
Mmm!

2202
01:23:23,365 --> 01:23:24,366
Mmm!

2203
01:23:25,367 --> 01:23:27,135
-This is good.
-Isn't it?

2204
01:23:27,202 --> 01:23:28,937
-It's so good.
-This is good.

2205
01:23:29,504 --> 01:23:31,239
-It's really good.
-It is.

2206
01:23:31,306 --> 01:23:33,742
-How did he do this?
-Ho-young really is

2207
01:23:33,808 --> 01:23:35,744
good at everything.

2208
01:23:36,444 --> 01:23:39,114
It's also the best <i>yum woon sen</i>
I have ever had.

2209
01:23:39,814 --> 01:23:40,648
It's so good.

2210
01:23:40,715 --> 01:23:42,450
You didn't use fish sauce, right?

2211
01:23:42,517 --> 01:23:46,287
She didn't have it,
but she had anchovy <i>aekjeot.</i>

2212
01:23:46,354 --> 01:23:48,523
<i>-So I made use of that.</i>
<i>-This is to die for.</i>

2213
01:23:49,491 --> 01:23:52,260
I like how it's not overly done.

2214
01:23:52,327 --> 01:23:57,032
And the way all of this seafood
is cooked is perfect.

2215
01:23:57,098 --> 01:23:59,300
I want to drink this sauce.

2216
01:24:00,335 --> 01:24:02,237
NEXT, PHILLY CHEESE SANDWICH

2217
01:24:02,871 --> 01:24:04,806
YUM

2218
01:24:07,242 --> 01:24:08,476
It's unbelievable, right?

2219
01:24:08,543 --> 01:24:10,445
GLARING

2220
01:24:10,512 --> 01:24:12,280
-What's wrong?
-Philly cheese steak.

2221
01:24:12,347 --> 01:24:14,215
-It's good.
-Can you start selling these?

2222
01:24:14,783 --> 01:24:16,751
THANK YOU

2223
01:24:16,818 --> 01:24:19,921
-Right?
-It's a shame that only we get to eat.

2224
01:24:19,988 --> 01:24:22,223
It's so good with the sauce.

2225
01:24:22,290 --> 01:24:23,458
CHOMP

2226
01:24:23,525 --> 01:24:25,460
This is too good.

2227
01:24:25,693 --> 01:24:26,895
ISN'T IT?

2228
01:24:26,961 --> 01:24:29,564
Next, Poong and Moon-jung's dish.

2229
01:24:29,631 --> 01:24:31,800
-I was curious.
-Chinese Poison.

2230
01:24:31,866 --> 01:24:34,135
This one looks pretty good too.

2231
01:24:34,202 --> 01:24:36,337
<i>Jjajangmyeon</i> and menbosha.

2232
01:24:36,404 --> 01:24:38,306
-It tastes like <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>
-It does.

2233
01:24:38,373 --> 01:24:39,607
It's <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

2234
01:24:39,674 --> 01:24:42,510
-It's just <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>
-It's <i>jjajangmyeon.</i> It's so good.

2235
01:24:42,577 --> 01:24:45,246
If I didn't see them cooking,
I wouldn't have known the difference.

2236
01:24:45,313 --> 01:24:46,848
It's so good.

2237
01:24:46,915 --> 01:24:48,483
It's really good.

2238
01:24:48,550 --> 01:24:50,618
DONE WITH THIS

2239
01:24:51,119 --> 01:24:52,654
MOVING ON TO THE LEFTOVER SAUCE

2240
01:24:55,290 --> 01:24:56,458
HMM?

2241
01:24:56,524 --> 01:24:58,693
-Rice…
-Do you need rice?

2242
01:24:58,760 --> 01:25:00,061
Rice, please.

2243
01:25:00,695 --> 01:25:01,529
This is hard.

2244
01:25:01,596 --> 01:25:03,364
Is this only possible
with homemade <i>doenjang?</i>

2245
01:25:03,431 --> 01:25:05,300
You can do it with store-bought ones,

2246
01:25:05,366 --> 01:25:07,102
but when you do that,

2247
01:25:07,168 --> 01:25:09,637
it's better to add a bit of flour to it.

2248
01:25:09,704 --> 01:25:12,040
It has that charred flavor.

2249
01:25:12,107 --> 01:25:13,308
-Smoky flavor.
-Smoky.

2250
01:25:13,374 --> 01:25:14,309
Maillard reaction.

2251
01:25:14,375 --> 01:25:16,711
-I tasted that smoky flavor.
-Smoky flavor.

2252
01:25:16,778 --> 01:25:18,913
I've often had <i>jjajang</i> sauce

2253
01:25:18,980 --> 01:25:20,215
made with <i>doenjang.</i>

2254
01:25:20,281 --> 01:25:22,817
And among those dishes,

2255
01:25:22,884 --> 01:25:25,286
this was the most similar
to actual <i>jjajang</i> sauce.

2256
01:25:25,353 --> 01:25:28,189
And when you have
really good <i>jjajangmyeon,</i>

2257
01:25:28,256 --> 01:25:30,458
-you need that grease coating your lips.
-Yes.

2258
01:25:30,525 --> 01:25:32,193
-That coat.
-And soon after a bite,

2259
01:25:32,260 --> 01:25:35,630
it was nice to feel
that coat of grease on my lips.

2260
01:25:35,697 --> 01:25:38,666
It tasted like
a delicious bowl of <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

2261
01:25:41,836 --> 01:25:43,905
Did you enjoy your elaborate meal?

2262
01:25:43,972 --> 01:25:45,607
She looks full.

2263
01:25:45,673 --> 01:25:47,075
My dress feels too tight now.

2264
01:25:48,476 --> 01:25:50,044
She had a lot.

2265
01:25:50,111 --> 01:25:52,480
-I still have the menbosha.
-The menbosha.

2266
01:25:53,548 --> 01:25:55,483
She'll have to choose soon.

2267
01:25:55,550 --> 01:25:58,720
The texture of the sourdough menbosha
is great.

2268
01:25:58,786 --> 01:26:01,923
-It's much better than regular bread.
-Much better, right?

2269
01:26:01,990 --> 01:26:03,191
Yes, this is really good.

2270
01:26:04,025 --> 01:26:05,326
MMM!

2271
01:26:05,393 --> 01:26:07,362
It's so hard to choose.

2272
01:26:07,428 --> 01:26:10,064
-It is. It's really hard.
-What do I do now?

2273
01:26:10,131 --> 01:26:12,500
<i>Press one for Sam and Ho-young,</i>

2274
01:26:12,567 --> 01:26:15,236
<i>and two for Poong and Moon-jung.</i>

2275
01:26:15,303 --> 01:26:16,704
Jung-hwa's choice.

2276
01:26:16,771 --> 01:26:18,907
Press the button.

2277
01:26:19,474 --> 01:26:21,809
My finger is going like this.

2278
01:26:22,777 --> 01:26:23,645
What do I do?

2279
01:26:23,711 --> 01:26:25,313
-Is it hard?
-It's hard.

2280
01:26:25,380 --> 01:26:26,781
I'll pick one.

2281
01:26:26,848 --> 01:26:28,049
Pick one.

2282
01:26:28,116 --> 01:26:29,350
Okay?

2283
01:26:29,417 --> 01:26:31,386
-Okay.
-Okay.

2284
01:26:31,452 --> 01:26:33,955
She pressed one now.

2285
01:26:34,722 --> 01:26:38,426
Which team did she choose?

2286
01:26:38,493 --> 01:26:40,361
Let's find out.

2287
01:26:40,428 --> 01:26:41,429
Show us.

2288
01:26:42,564 --> 01:26:45,900
That was "Junky Low-Carb, Low-Sugar,"

2289
01:26:45,967 --> 01:26:48,036
played as a relay round, a tag team round.

2290
01:26:48,102 --> 01:26:49,837
Will it be Poong and Moon-jung?

2291
01:26:49,904 --> 01:26:52,040
-Or Ho-young and Sam?
-And Sam?

2292
01:26:52,106 --> 01:26:54,409
Will Ho-young and Sam

2293
01:26:54,475 --> 01:26:56,811
-get their revenge on Poong?
-Please.

2294
01:26:56,878 --> 01:26:59,881
Or will Poong and Moon-jung

2295
01:26:59,948 --> 01:27:01,983
win another star?

2296
01:27:02,650 --> 01:27:05,320
Who won?

2297
01:27:05,386 --> 01:27:07,088
Who did she choose?

2298
01:27:07,155 --> 01:27:08,690
Who is it?

2299
01:27:08,756 --> 01:27:09,757
Who is it?

2300
01:27:09,824 --> 01:27:11,759
KIM POONG AND LEE MOON-JUNG WIN

2301
01:27:12,193 --> 01:27:15,029
KIM POONG AND LEE MOON-JUNG'S
CHINESE POISON WINS

2302
01:27:15,096 --> 01:27:16,097
Poong and Moon-jung.

2303
01:27:16,164 --> 01:27:17,532
EXCITED

2304
01:27:19,167 --> 01:27:20,735
That <i>jjajangmyeon</i> was tough to beat.

2305
01:27:23,438 --> 01:27:25,607
It was so hard.
Choosing was very hard for both rounds.

2306
01:27:25,673 --> 01:27:27,875
-This is way too good.
-It's still hard.

2307
01:27:27,942 --> 01:27:29,244
I put the focus

2308
01:27:29,310 --> 01:27:32,113
on which ones felt more junky.

2309
01:27:32,180 --> 01:27:33,848
Yes, it's so junky.

2310
01:27:33,915 --> 01:27:38,586
Also, it was meaningful to me
that my mom's <i>doenjang</i>

2311
01:27:38,653 --> 01:27:42,090
can turn into <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

2312
01:27:42,156 --> 01:27:44,859
I always crave it so much
when I'm on a diet,

2313
01:27:44,926 --> 01:27:47,996
so it was great to know
I can make it low-carb, low-sugar.

2314
01:27:48,062 --> 01:27:49,998
It was really touching.

2315
01:27:50,064 --> 01:27:51,699
That was my reasoning.

2316
01:27:53,067 --> 01:27:54,302
THANK YOU

2317
01:27:54,369 --> 01:27:56,971
Now, with Moon-jung next to you,

2318
01:27:57,038 --> 01:27:59,107
how do you feel, Poong?

2319
01:27:59,173 --> 01:28:02,343
When Hyun-suk and I played as a team,

2320
01:28:02,410 --> 01:28:04,445
we had won together,
and we won again today.

2321
01:28:04,512 --> 01:28:06,547
I might be the victory fairy.

2322
01:28:07,982 --> 01:28:09,284
-Just a thought.
-The victory fairy.

2323
01:28:09,350 --> 01:28:11,019
How brazen of you.

2324
01:28:11,085 --> 01:28:12,487
It all goes to Moon-jung.

2325
01:28:12,553 --> 01:28:15,356
She gave them a really good fight.

2326
01:28:15,423 --> 01:28:18,559
Please put the stars
on Poong and Moon-jung.

2327
01:28:19,594 --> 01:28:21,095
Great job.

2328
01:28:22,830 --> 01:28:26,167
That was Poong's ninth win,
and Moon-jung's fourth win.

2329
01:28:26,234 --> 01:28:28,002
-Already?
-Congratulations!

2330
01:28:28,069 --> 01:28:30,571
-Thank you.
-They win the team round.

2331
01:28:30,638 --> 01:28:32,774
-Congratulations.
-Look at him.

2332
01:28:32,840 --> 01:28:33,775
COMING UP: THE PREVIEW

2333
01:28:34,309 --> 01:28:35,410
Is it your birthday?

2334
01:28:35,476 --> 01:28:36,778
Wait, are you 010…

2335
01:28:36,844 --> 01:28:37,979
The love story starts there.

2336
01:28:38,046 --> 01:28:39,914
By any chance, do you like Chapaguri?

2337
01:28:39,981 --> 01:28:41,549
-Strip loin.
-With strip loin?

2338
01:28:42,250 --> 01:28:43,351
Cut!

2339
01:28:43,651 --> 01:28:45,353
TWO VETERAN ACTORS
CHO YEO-JEONG & HA SEOK-JIN

2340
01:28:45,420 --> 01:28:47,488
This is the 30th year since her debut.

2341
01:28:47,555 --> 01:28:49,290
What's the secret
behind your youthfulness?

2342
01:28:49,357 --> 01:28:50,925
I hold back, reluctantly.

2343
01:28:50,992 --> 01:28:52,093
I eat <i>jjajangmyeon</i> and <i>ramyeon</i>

2344
01:28:52,160 --> 01:28:53,261
probably twice a year.

2345
01:28:53,461 --> 01:28:54,362
SHOCKED

2346
01:28:54,429 --> 01:28:55,530
I can't live like that.

2347
01:28:55,596 --> 01:28:57,298
-Are you looking for healthy--
-No!

2348
01:28:57,598 --> 01:28:58,700
THE MOST URGENT SHOUT

2349
01:28:58,766 --> 01:29:01,135
I want to eat a lot
even if it's loaded with calories.

2350
01:29:01,402 --> 01:29:02,270
A ROUND FOR CHO YEO-JEONG,

2351
01:29:02,337 --> 01:29:03,638
DISHES LOADED WITH CALORIES

2352
01:29:03,905 --> 01:29:05,039
RAISE HER SUPPRESSED APPETITE

2353
01:29:05,406 --> 01:29:06,607
DON'T HOLD BACK ON HER FAVORITES

2354
01:29:06,808 --> 01:29:07,642
WOW

2355
01:29:07,875 --> 01:29:08,910
IT'S SO EXCITING

2356
01:29:09,911 --> 01:29:11,412
MERCILESS AMOUNT OF OIL

2357
01:29:11,746 --> 01:29:13,514
NO LIMIT ON CALORIES

2358
01:29:13,781 --> 01:29:14,615
EXPLODING WITH EXCITEMENT

2359
01:29:14,682 --> 01:29:15,750
-My gosh.
-That cheese.

2360
01:29:16,184 --> 01:29:18,920
GOING COMPLETELY RECKLESS

2361
01:29:19,487 --> 01:29:21,789
WHICH DISH BROKE
HER 30 YEARS OF DISCIPLINE?

2362
01:29:21,856 --> 01:29:23,358
She loves it so much.

2363
01:29:26,094 --> 01:29:27,662
Isn't it good?

2364
01:29:27,729 --> 01:29:29,263
It's so good.

2365
01:29:39,707 --> 01:29:44,712
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
